@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Styles, themes and fonts)

A stylesheet is the theme: named values, text styles and box styles. This collection uses styles/IDocDemo.style, applied by the first line of every file.

@section(Stylesheets)

@subsection(@@style)

Apply a stylesheet: a bare name finds styles/Name.style.

@style(IDocDemo)

@style(IDocDemo, titles=Helvetica, h1.size=24pt)

@style(IDocDemo)

@style(IDocDemo)

@style(IDocDemo, test="Quiz 1")
H@sub(2)O

@subsection(@@value)

A stylesheet's named values, written once: value(basefont=Times Roman, titles=Arial, basesize=12pt).

@value(basefont=Times Roman, titles=Arial, basesize=12pt, ink=#1f3a5f)

@subsection(@@textstyle)

Typography for a named role, set once, honored on screen AND in the PDF.

@textstyle(normal, font="Georgia", size=18pt)

@textstyle(normal, indent=1.5em, spacing=0.4em, leading=1.6)

@textstyle(title, size=28pt)

@textstyle(table, font=Palatino, size=9pt)

@textstyle(tableheader, color=#1f3a5f)

@textstyle(h1, extends=title, size=20pt)

@textstyle(huge, extends=normal, size=1.5em, weight=bold)

@textstyle(subsection, number=0)

@textstyle(title, font=titles, color=ink)

@textstyle(note1, extends=normal, align=center, fg=#065f46, bgcolor=#ecfdf5)

@textstyle(note2, extends=normal, fgcolor=#7c2d12, background=#fff7ed, italic, hang=2em, paragraphstyle=space)

@use(note1) Centred green words from a named style. @end

@use(note2) Italic, hanging, on a warm background. @end

@textstyle(alleft, extends=normal, align=left)

@textstyle(alright, extends=normal, align=right)

@textstyle(aljustify, extends=normal, align=justify)

@textstyle(face0, extends=normal, font=Times New Roman)
@use(face0) This line is set in Times New Roman. @end

@textstyle(face1, extends=normal, font=Garamond)
@use(face1) This line is set in Garamond. @end

@textstyle(face2, extends=normal, font=Arial)
@use(face2) This line is set in Arial. @end

@textstyle(face3, extends=normal, font=Helvetica)
@use(face3) This line is set in Helvetica. @end

@textstyle(face4, extends=normal, font=Calibri)
@use(face4) This line is set in Calibri. @end

@textstyle(face5, extends=normal, font=Computer Modern)
@use(face5) This line is set in Computer Modern. @end

@textstyle(face6, extends=normal, font=serif)
@use(face6) This line is set in serif. @end

@textstyle(face7, extends=normal, font=sans)
@use(face7) This line is set in sans. @end

@subsection(@@use)

Put a style of the stylesheet's own on words, up to end: textstyle(huge, extends=normal, size=1.5em, weight=bold) names it (any name that is not a role), use(huge) puts it on.

@use(huge)
A whole paragraph.
@end

@subsection(@@inherits)

Inside a .style: splice the parent stylesheet in first, so this sheet's settings override it.

@inherits(IDocDemo)

@subsection(@@theme)

Pin a named colour theme for THIS document (the reader can still override it in Appearance).

@theme(nord)

@theme(code, monokai)
The gain is 12 dB @todo(Check this value) at 1 kHz.
